{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"SB0312","billNumberShort":"S.B. 312","billNumberLong":"SB0312S01","fileNumber":"2026FL1447","shortTitle":"Educator License Amendments","currentSubVersion":"1","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"JOHNSJD","primeSponsorName":"Sen. Johnson, John D.","primeSponsorHouse":"S","floorSponsor":"WELTOD","floorSponsorName":"Rep. Welton, Doug","floorSponsorHouse":"H","generalProvisions":"This bill modifies provisions relating to educator license discipline and restrictions on employment and volunteer service.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>amends provisions relating to ineligibility for educator licensure following license denial;<hr><ltbullet>establishes a tiered framework for restrictions on employment and volunteer service following license suspension or revocation;<hr><ltbullet>requires automatic restrictions for serious misconduct involving actual harm or credible risk to children;<hr><ltbullet>requires written findings demonstrating specific risk for restrictions in other cases;<hr><ltbullet>exempts technical violations from automatic work and volunteer restrictions;<hr><ltbullet>enacts provisions governing restrictions on employment and volunteer service following disciplinary action;<hr><ltbullet>modifies notice requirements for disciplinary proceedings; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Jeff Van Hulten","fiscalAnalyst":"Kiki Hudson","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/26/2026","trackingID":"SRQPOAUVMU","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-02-19 12:26:03.393","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owne